# Generated output. `yarn format` rewrites whatever it is pointed at, and rewriting a
# build artefact only makes the next build's diff noisy. ESLint ignores the same two
# directories, so the formatting gate and the fixer agree on what is source.
dist/
coverage/

# Rendered from openapi.yaml by `yarn openapi`, and the suite asserts it is exactly what
# that renderer writes (src/openapi/openapi.spec.ts). Prettier fills arrays to its print
# width where JSON.stringify puts one element per line, so formatting this file would put
# the two checks at odds — and the authoritative document, which Prettier *does* format,
# is the YAML beside it.
openapi.json

# The result parser's fixture matrix (#329): uploaded reports held byte for byte — one is
# deliberately cut mid-document, which Prettier would refuse or "repair" — and the golden
# file its suite writes.
src/modules/test-results/fixtures/

# The detection certification's golden file (#389), as `GoldenFile.save` writes it — one array
# element per line, where Prettier would fill short arrays to its print width. Formatting it
# would make every regeneration a diff of whitespace.
src/modules/detection/detection.archetypes.golden.json

# The digest's golden renders (#440), as `GoldenFile.save` writes them. The HTML parts are
# single-line strings the screenshot suite loads as they are.
src/modules/insights/digest/digest.golden.json
